The Developer reserves the right to terminate your access to the multiplayer servers at any time, for any reason, without notice.

3. PRIVACY (GDPR)
This game does not use cookies or advertising IDs and does not collect data that directly identifies you (such as your name, email address, or account details).
Single-player mode is fully playable offline. A network connection is only required for the multiplayer mode and for an anonymous startup usage ping (see below).
Connecting to the multiplayer servers requires transmitting your IP address. This data is processed strictly for the legitimate interest of establishing the network connection, syncing game state, and maintaining server security. IP addresses are not used for advertising and are only kept in temporary security/usage logs.
For statistical purposes, in order to estimate the number of users, data about connections is temporarily logged on the server.
The game generates a random identifier (UID) stored locally on your device the first time you launch it. This UID is not derived from your name, email, hardware, or any account, and is a pseudonymous identifier not linked to your real-world identity. It is transmitted to the server and used only for the legitimate interest of producing aggregate usage and player-retention statistics. You have the right to access or request erasure of data associated with your UID by contacting the Developer (see section 7).

